From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fixture Developer <dev@mobimanual.local>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Let helpdesk staff install iOS updates

Most "my iPad needs the update" tickets land with the helpdesk, who had
to hand each one to an administrator. Helpdesk may now send Update OS.

Retire and Wipe stay with administrators.
---
Expected: worth documenting. Triage answers doc-impact. A one-line permission change that makes two tables wrong: the draft adds Update OS to the Helpdesk row of the Roles table on _users.md, and Helpdesk to the Update OS row on _devicescommands.md.
Expected-outcome: opened
Expected-edits: _users.md _devicescommands.md

 server/auth/permissions.js | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/auth/permissions.js b/server/auth/permissions.js
index 7f8b6f2..68a1564 100644
--- a/server/auth/permissions.js
+++ b/server/auth/permissions.js
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ const ROLES = {
   administrator: ['*'],
   helpdesk: [
     'devices.read', 'devices.move', 'devices.department',
-    'commands.lock', 'commands.ring', 'commands.clear-passcode',
+    'commands.lock', 'commands.ring', 'commands.clear-passcode', 'commands.update-os',
     'groups.read', 'policies.read', 'apps.read', 'users.read'
   ],
   auditor: [
